---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

const description = 'An enthusiast’s airgun reviews, testing notes, maintenance experiences, and comparisons, based on personal use and observations.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About`} description={description} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>About</h1>
			<p>
				{SITE_TITLE} is my personal blog about airgun reviews, testing, maintenance,
				and comparisons. I share firsthand impressions, photos, and measurements
				from the airguns I use, offering one owner’s perspective on what they
				are like.
			</p>
			<h2>Why I created it</h2>
			<p>
				This site grew out of my personal interest in airguns. Before buying one,
				I often wanted more detail than I could find: how the grip feels, how the
				trigger behaves, what maintenance involves, and how it compares with
				similar models. Specifications help, but they only tell part of the story.
			</p>
			<p>
				I created {SITE_TITLE} to share the detailed, practical observations I was
				looking for. My goal is to make comparisons useful by explaining both
				what I measured and what I experienced.
			</p>
			<p>
				I’m working toward a more systematic, evidence-based approach to comparing
				airguns. My aim is to make tests more repeatable, describe the conditions
				and methods used, and distinguish personal impressions from measurements.
				These are hobbyist tests, and I’ll refine my approach as I learn.
			</p>
			<h2>Who am I?</h2>
			<p>
				I'm an airgun enthusiast and recreational player.
				I became interested in airguns through precision target competition and gradually
				started testing different pneumatic and spring-powered airguns.
			</p>
			<h2>A note on the content</h2>
			<p>
				My observations relate to the particular airguns, setups, and conditions
				I describe. Results and impressions may differ for other examples or
				players, and they are not guarantees of performance or suitability.
			</p>
			<p>
				Maintenance articles document my own experience. They are not a substitute
				for the manufacturer’s instructions or advice from a qualified technician.
				Follow the manufacturer’s safety guidance and check the laws that apply
				where you live.
			</p>
			<h2>Get in touch</h2>
			<p>
				Have a question, correction, or an airgun experience to share? Email me at <a href="mailto:hello@airguncraft.com?subject=%5BAirgun%20Craft%5D%20Hello">hello@airguncraft.com</a>.
				I’d love to hear from fellow enthusiasts.
			</p>
			<p><a href="/">Read the blog</a></p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
